{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2017-717", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2017/717", "wordCount": 4056, "segments": [{"start": 17.0, "text": "Hello, I'm Tanya Kancheva and"}, {"start": 19.0, "text": "I'm here to talk about wireless"}, {"start": 21.0, "text": "CarPlay."}, {"start": 23.0, "text": "wireless CarPlay is perfect for"}, {"start": 25.0, "text": "any trip, you can get in your"}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "car without taking your iPhone"}, {"start": 29.0, "text": "out of your bag or pocket and"}, {"start": 32.0, "text": "start experiencing CarPlay"}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "effortlessly."}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "The CarPlay experience is the"}, {"start": 37.0, "text": "same whether you are plugged in"}, {"start": 39.0, "text": "or using it wirelessly."}, {"start": 42.0, "text": "In this session, we will dive"}, {"start": 44.0, "text": "into the details on developing a"}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "wireless CarPlay system."}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "First, let's start by talking"}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "about the wireless CarPlay"}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "experience."}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "The first time you use wireless"}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "CarPlay you need to pair your"}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "iPhone to your car."}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "The simplest way to pair is by"}, {"start": 66.0, "text": "plugging in iPhone using a"}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "cable."}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "You can also pair without"}, {"start": 70.0, "text": "plugging in by using the car's"}, {"start": 72.0, "text": "UI to add a new device and by"}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "following the onscreen"}, {"start": 76.0, "text": "instructions."}, {"start": 79.0, "text": "Plugging in iPhone using a cable"}, {"start": 81.0, "text": "is the easiest and fastest way"}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "to pair for wireless CarPlay and"}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "all wireless CarPlay systems"}, {"start": 88.0, "text": "should support this feature."}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "When iPhone is plugged in"}, {"start": 92.0, "text": "CarPlay starts normally."}, {"start": 95.0, "text": "If the car supports wireless"}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "CarPlay the user will be"}, {"start": 98.0, "text": "presented with the following"}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "prompt on iPhone."}, {"start": 104.0, "text": "A simple tap on enable wireless"}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "CarPlay completes the pairing"}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "process."}, {"start": 109.0, "text": "Be sure to provide a meaningful"}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "display name as in this example,"}, {"start": 114.0, "text": "my car, so it's clear that"}, {"start": 117.0, "text": "iPhone will be associated with"}, {"start": 118.0, "text": "the car."}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "Once pairing is complete CarPlay"}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "starts automatically the next"}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "time you enter the car."}, {"start": 129.0, "text": "It's not necessary to require"}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "additional confirmation on the"}, {"start": 133.0, "text": "car's display because CarPlay is"}, {"start": 135.0, "text": "already running and the user has"}, {"start": 138.0, "text": "already chosen to use wireless"}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "CarPlay on iPhone."}, {"start": 142.0, "text": "As you can see, pairing by"}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "plugging in is simple and"}, {"start": 147.0, "text": "effortless."}, {"start": 150.0, "text": "The user can also pair without"}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "plugging in and by using the"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "car's UI to add a new device and"}, {"start": 156.0, "text": "by following the onscreen"}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "instructions."}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "To begin, the pairing process"}, {"start": 162.0, "text": "needs to be started on both the"}, {"start": 163.0, "text": "car and on iPhone."}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "To make it easier CarPlay"}, {"start": 170.0, "text": "standardizes a long press on the"}, {"start": 173.0, "text": "Voice Control button to start"}, {"start": 175.0, "text": "the pairing process."}, {"start": 177.0, "text": "Normally this will start Siri,"}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "but if no phone is connected the"}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "car should immediately prepare"}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "for pairing."}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "You can also use menus and"}, {"start": 186.0, "text": "settings in the car's native UI"}, {"start": 188.0, "text": "to start the pairing process."}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "You may offer a CarPlay specific"}, {"start": 192.0, "text": "menu, a general Bluetooth menu"}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "or both."}, {"start": 198.0, "text": "In CarPlay settings on iPhone"}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "users are encouraged to press"}, {"start": 202.0, "text": "and hold the Voice Control"}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "button on the steering wheel to"}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "start the pairing process."}, {"start": 209.0, "text": "Once CarPlay setup is started on"}, {"start": 212.0, "text": "the car and iPhone select the"}, {"start": 214.0, "text": "discovered device to start the"}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "pairing process."}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "Apple recommends that you allow"}, {"start": 221.0, "text": "the user to select the car from"}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "iPhone."}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "In your native UI simply show"}, {"start": 227.0, "text": "your car's display name so the"}, {"start": 229.0, "text": "user knows what to look for."}, {"start": 234.0, "text": "If you do allow the user to"}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "initiate selection from the car"}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "you can show a list of"}, {"start": 239.0, "text": "discovered devices."}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "You can show a less specific to"}, {"start": 243.0, "text": "adding a CarPlay device or you"}, {"start": 247.0, "text": "can show a list of all"}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "discovered Bluetooth devices,"}, {"start": 250.0, "text": "including CarPlay devices."}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "If the user selects a device"}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "using a general Bluetooth menu"}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "and that device supports"}, {"start": 260.0, "text": "wireless CarPlay, you may decide"}, {"start": 262.0, "text": "to offer to enable CarPlay."}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "Do not show this screen if the"}, {"start": 266.0, "text": "user selected the device from a"}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "CarPlay specific menu."}, {"start": 272.0, "text": "Then CarPlay connects and"}, {"start": 275.0, "text": "CarPlay appears on the screen."}, {"start": 277.0, "text": "From here on the CarPlay"}, {"start": 279.0, "text": "experience is the same as"}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "plugging in until you leave the"}, {"start": 282.0, "text": "car."}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "Every time the user enters the"}, {"start": 288.0, "text": "car CarPlay reconnects"}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "automatically, iPhone can remain"}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "in your bag or pocket and no"}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "user interaction is necessary."}, {"start": 299.0, "text": "When CarPlay starts, be sure to"}, {"start": 301.0, "text": "observe the last user mode for"}, {"start": 303.0, "text": "audio in the display."}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "For details, watch the video"}, {"start": 308.0, "text": "Developing CarPlay Systems Part"}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "1."}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "With wireless CarPlay it's easy"}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "to pair more than one iPhone"}, {"start": 319.0, "text": "with the car."}, {"start": 321.0, "text": "In addition, you may have one or"}, {"start": 323.0, "text": "many iPhones plugged in at the"}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "same time."}, {"start": 328.0, "text": "Provide a device selector in"}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "your native UI that lets the"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "user choose the active CarPlay"}, {"start": 334.0, "text": "device."}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "Once CarPlay has started don't"}, {"start": 338.0, "text": "automatically switch to another"}, {"start": 339.0, "text": "device."}, {"start": 341.0, "text": "Changing the active CarPlay"}, {"start": 342.0, "text": "device should be an explicit"}, {"start": 344.0, "text": "user action."}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "If you support multiple"}, {"start": 348.0, "text": "Bluetooth devices and have a"}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "concept of favorite or"}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "frequently used devices use the"}, {"start": 355.0, "text": "same mechanism for wireless"}, {"start": 357.0, "text": "CarPlay."}, {"start": 359.0, "text": "Your device selector shows all"}, {"start": 362.0, "text": "CarPlay devices whether they are"}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "plugged in or paired for"}, {"start": 366.0, "text": "wireless CarPlay."}, {"start": 368.0, "text": "Indicate the active CarPlay"}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "device using the CarPlay logo."}, {"start": 373.0, "text": "Never indicate if CarPlay is"}, {"start": 375.0, "text": "running over wireless or wired."}, {"start": 378.0, "text": "The transfer type should be"}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "transparent to the user."}, {"start": 382.0, "text": "If you provide on off settings"}, {"start": 385.0, "text": "don't provide separate settings"}, {"start": 386.0, "text": "for wired and wireless CarPlay,"}, {"start": 388.0, "text": "just provide a setting for"}, {"start": 390.0, "text": "Bluetooth or iPod versus"}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "CarPlay."}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "Be judicious in showing"}, {"start": 395.0, "text": "notifications, only show"}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "notifications when it's"}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "important to let the users know."}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "Show a subtle notification when"}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "the first iPhone is connected"}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "only if CarPlay will not"}, {"start": 408.0, "text": "immediately become visible or"}, {"start": 411.0, "text": "the CarPlay icon is"}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "not immediately visible."}, {"start": 416.0, "text": "Show a notification when a"}, {"start": 417.0, "text": "second iPhone is connected over"}, {"start": 420.0, "text": "USB while CarPlay is running."}, {"start": 423.0, "text": "Do not show notifications when"}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "iPhone joins or leaves the"}, {"start": 428.0, "text": "access point or when it is"}, {"start": 430.0, "text": "reconnected over Bluetooth."}, {"start": 435.0, "text": "Now that we have seen how to use"}, {"start": 437.0, "text": "wireless CarPlay let's explore"}, {"start": 440.0, "text": "what it takes to develop such a"}, {"start": 441.0, "text": "system."}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "We'll start with the hardware"}, {"start": 446.0, "text": "requirements, go through setup"}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "and pairing, reconnecting for"}, {"start": 450.0, "text": "CarPlay, and finish with some"}, {"start": 453.0, "text": "considerations for your wireless"}, {"start": 455.0, "text": "architecture."}, {"start": 458.0, "text": "So, hardware requirements."}, {"start": 460.0, "text": "wireless CarPlay requires"}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "Bluetooth, a Wi-Fi access point"}, {"start": 464.0, "text": "and location data."}, {"start": 467.0, "text": "Bluetooth is used to discover"}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "and reconnect CarPlay devices."}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "To accomplish this the Bluetooth"}, {"start": 475.0, "text": "subsystem needs to implement the"}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "Bluetooth core specification, as"}, {"start": 479.0, "text": "well as support service"}, {"start": 480.0, "text": "discovery, iAP2 protocols and"}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "advertise CarPlay support in its"}, {"start": 486.0, "text": "Bluetooth Extended Inquiry"}, {"start": 487.0, "text": "Response."}, {"start": 491.0, "text": "The Wi-Fi link is used for all"}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "audio and video transfer to the"}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "CarPlay protocol, as well as"}, {"start": 499.0, "text": "iAP2 data transfer."}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "The access point must be"}, {"start": 503.0, "text": "certified by the Wi-Fi Alliance"}, {"start": 505.0, "text": "and it is recommended that it"}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "supports the 802.11ac standard"}, {"start": 511.0, "text": "and operates in the 5GHz"}, {"start": 513.0, "text": "frequency band."}, {"start": 515.0, "text": "In addition, the axis point"}, {"start": 517.0, "text": "needs to support the Apple"}, {"start": 519.0, "text": "Device Information Element and"}, {"start": 521.0, "text": "the Interworking Information"}, {"start": 524.0, "text": "Element."}, {"start": 525.0, "text": "The location has always been"}, {"start": 527.0, "text": "required for CarPlay, but it"}, {"start": 529.0, "text": "becomes an absolute necessity"}, {"start": 532.0, "text": "with wireless CarPlay as the"}, {"start": 534.0, "text": "driver's phone might be left in"}, {"start": 535.0, "text": "a pocket or a bag and be"}, {"start": 537.0, "text": "completely out of sight."}, {"start": 540.0, "text": "To provide reliable and precise"}, {"start": 542.0, "text": "location data, the head unit"}, {"start": 544.0, "text": "needs a GNSS receiver, access to"}, {"start": 548.0, "text": "the speed sensor of the vehicle,"}, {"start": 550.0, "text": "as well as the ability to"}, {"start": 551.0, "text": "provide dead reckoning position"}, {"start": 553.0, "text": "information."}, {"start": 555.0, "text": "Okay, now that we have talked"}, {"start": 557.0, "text": "through the basic hardware"}, {"start": 558.0, "text": "requirements let's talk about"}, {"start": 560.0, "text": "set up and pairing for CarPlay."}, {"start": 565.0, "text": "First, let's look at what"}, {"start": 567.0, "text": "components are needed to set up"}, {"start": 569.0, "text": "wireless and wired CarPlay."}, {"start": 573.0, "text": "Of course, one or many USB"}, {"start": 575.0, "text": "ports, a Wi-Fi access point,"}, {"start": 579.0, "text": "Bluetooth module, and an"}, {"start": 581.0, "text": "instance of the CarPlay"}, {"start": 583.0, "text": "communication plugin are"}, {"start": 584.0, "text": "required."}, {"start": 587.0, "text": "On ignition on or a head unit"}, {"start": 589.0, "text": "restart the components need to"}, {"start": 591.0, "text": "be initialized and set up."}, {"start": 594.0, "text": "USBs ready for role swap and NCM"}, {"start": 597.0, "text": "communication for wired CarPlay."}, {"start": 600.0, "text": "BT, Wi-Fi and networking for"}, {"start": 602.0, "text": "wireless CarPlay."}, {"start": 604.0, "text": "Bonjour and the communication"}, {"start": 607.0, "text": "plugin to enable CarPlay"}, {"start": 609.0, "text": "discovery."}, {"start": 611.0, "text": "When all those components are"}, {"start": 613.0, "text": "set up the system is ready for"}, {"start": 615.0, "text": "CarPlay connection."}, {"start": 618.0, "text": "As we saw earlier, there are two"}, {"start": 620.0, "text": "ways to pair iPhone to the car."}, {"start": 623.0, "text": "If iPhone is plugged in using a"}, {"start": 625.0, "text": "cable out-of-band pairing is"}, {"start": 628.0, "text": "triggered in the background."}, {"start": 631.0, "text": "Otherwise, a Bluetooth pairing"}, {"start": 633.0, "text": "process is needed."}, {"start": 636.0, "text": "Setup over USB requires less"}, {"start": 639.0, "text": "user interaction and is the"}, {"start": 641.0, "text": "recommended setup procedure."}, {"start": 646.0, "text": "Now let's dive into pairing over"}, {"start": 648.0, "text": "USB."}, {"start": 650.0, "text": "As you see in the diagram, we"}, {"start": 652.0, "text": "have the essential head unit"}, {"start": 654.0, "text": "components on the left-hand side"}, {"start": 657.0, "text": "and iPhone is displayed on the"}, {"start": 659.0, "text": "right."}, {"start": 660.0, "text": "At this point, the system is"}, {"start": 662.0, "text": "fully booted and ready for"}, {"start": 664.0, "text": "CarPlay."}, {"start": 665.0, "text": "The head unit is showing the"}, {"start": 667.0, "text": "native user interface as the"}, {"start": 669.0, "text": "user connects over USB."}, {"start": 672.0, "text": "A USB role switch follows and"}, {"start": 676.0, "text": "iPhone shows that CarPlay's"}, {"start": 677.0, "text": "connected."}, {"start": 681.0, "text": "With the role switch the unit"}, {"start": 683.0, "text": "also establishes an iAP2 link"}, {"start": 686.0, "text": "declaring support for all"}, {"start": 688.0, "text": "necessary messages."}, {"start": 690.0, "text": "While the CarPlay session is"}, {"start": 692.0, "text": "starting over USB iPhone asks"}, {"start": 695.0, "text": "the user to enable wireless"}, {"start": 696.0, "text": "CarPlay."}, {"start": 700.0, "text": "With that CarPlay over USB is"}, {"start": 703.0, "text": "already active."}, {"start": 705.0, "text": "So, iOS proceeds with setting up"}, {"start": 708.0, "text": "the audio and video streams to"}, {"start": 710.0, "text": "show CarPlay in the car."}, {"start": 715.0, "text": "Now the user decides to enable"}, {"start": 717.0, "text": "wireless CarPlay."}, {"start": 721.0, "text": "After user confirmation iOS"}, {"start": 725.0, "text": "generates a Bluetooth link key"}, {"start": 727.0, "text": "and sends it over iAP to the"}, {"start": 729.0, "text": "unit."}, {"start": 731.0, "text": "The head unit saves the link key"}, {"start": 733.0, "text": "together with the device"}, {"start": 734.0, "text": "transport identifiers and stores"}, {"start": 737.0, "text": "this iPhone as a Bluetooth"}, {"start": 739.0, "text": "paired device set up for"}, {"start": 741.0, "text": "CarPlay."}, {"start": 744.0, "text": "Once the device is saved the"}, {"start": 747.0, "text": "head unit sends back a"}, {"start": 748.0, "text": "confirmation and out-of-band"}, {"start": 750.0, "text": "pairing is complete."}, {"start": 755.0, "text": "Let's review."}, {"start": 758.0, "text": "Without out-of-band pairing the"}, {"start": 761.0, "text": "CarPlay session is established"}, {"start": 762.0, "text": "over USB and is not interrupted."}, {"start": 767.0, "text": "There is no actual exchange over"}, {"start": 770.0, "text": "BT during this process."}, {"start": 774.0, "text": "The device needs to be stored as"}, {"start": 776.0, "text": "the last connected BT device or"}, {"start": 779.0, "text": "preferred device so that it can"}, {"start": 781.0, "text": "be reconnected later on."}, {"start": 785.0, "text": "Hence, a wireless CarPlay"}, {"start": 787.0, "text": "session will start automatically"}, {"start": 789.0, "text": "only after an ignition cycle as"}, {"start": 791.0, "text": "the driver returns to the car."}, {"start": 795.0, "text": "It's important to note that you"}, {"start": 798.0, "text": "should not start wireless"}, {"start": 799.0, "text": "CarPlay when the driver"}, {"start": 801.0, "text": "disconnects from USB, she might"}, {"start": 803.0, "text": "be just leaving the car."}, {"start": 806.0, "text": "Now that we have seen the USB"}, {"start": 808.0, "text": "setup for wireless CarPlay let's"}, {"start": 810.0, "text": "take a look at the second"}, {"start": 812.0, "text": "method, pairing over Bluetooth."}, {"start": 815.0, "text": "There are a couple of ways to"}, {"start": 817.0, "text": "initiate Bluetooth pairing in a"}, {"start": 818.0, "text": "vehicle."}, {"start": 820.0, "text": "A long press on the Voice"}, {"start": 822.0, "text": "Recognition button on the"}, {"start": 823.0, "text": "steering wheel or through the"}, {"start": 826.0, "text": "native UI."}, {"start": 829.0, "text": "And with the native UI there are"}, {"start": 831.0, "text": "two options. A dedicated UI for adding a"}, {"start": 835.0, "text": "CarPlay device or through the"}, {"start": 838.0, "text": "already existing UI for adding a"}, {"start": 840.0, "text": "BT device."}, {"start": 842.0, "text": "Over the next couple of slides,"}, {"start": 844.0, "text": "we will look into the"}, {"start": 845.0, "text": "differences between these"}, {"start": 847.0, "text": "pairing methods."}, {"start": 851.0, "text": "No matter which of the three"}, {"start": 853.0, "text": "pairing UIs was used by the"}, {"start": 855.0, "text": "driver to initiate pairing the"}, {"start": 858.0, "text": "head unit becomes discoverable."}, {"start": 861.0, "text": "The driver also needs to open"}, {"start": 863.0, "text": "either Bluetooth settings or"}, {"start": 866.0, "text": "CarPlay settings on iPhone to"}, {"start": 869.0, "text": "set iOS in a Bluetooth"}, {"start": 871.0, "text": "discoverable mode as well."}, {"start": 874.0, "text": "Again, this is a very generic"}, {"start": 877.0, "text": "representation of the fact that"}, {"start": 879.0, "text": "both the phone and the head unit"}, {"start": 880.0, "text": "must be set into a discoverable"}, {"start": 882.0, "text": "mode."}, {"start": 886.0, "text": "Now let's look at the different"}, {"start": 888.0, "text": "options on how to set up the"}, {"start": 891.0, "text": "head unit into a discoverable"}, {"start": 892.0, "text": "mode and how to select which"}, {"start": 894.0, "text": "device to pair to."}, {"start": 898.0, "text": "In this first variation, the"}, {"start": 899.0, "text": "head unit simply asks the user"}, {"start": 902.0, "text": "to search for the car's name on"}, {"start": 904.0, "text": "the CarPlay or BT settings menus"}, {"start": 907.0, "text": "on iPhone."}, {"start": 909.0, "text": "The user enters this menu by"}, {"start": 912.0, "text": "either navigating the native UI"}, {"start": 914.0, "text": "to add a new Bluetooth device or"}, {"start": 917.0, "text": "by long pressing on the Voice"}, {"start": 918.0, "text": "Recognition button on the"}, {"start": 920.0, "text": "steering wheel."}, {"start": 922.0, "text": "iPhone discovers the car and"}, {"start": 924.0, "text": "lists it."}, {"start": 928.0, "text": "The driver can then select the"}, {"start": 930.0, "text": "car on iPhone and iOS initiates"}, {"start": 934.0, "text": "a Bluetooth pairing request."}, {"start": 937.0, "text": "This is the simplest and most"}, {"start": 939.0, "text": "straightforward approach to"}, {"start": 941.0, "text": "accomplish Bluetooth pairing."}, {"start": 943.0, "text": "The second option is for the"}, {"start": 945.0, "text": "driver to select the device from"}, {"start": 947.0, "text": "a list of available Bluetooth"}, {"start": 949.0, "text": "devices on the car's native"}, {"start": 951.0, "text": "interface."}, {"start": 954.0, "text": "In this case, the head unit is"}, {"start": 956.0, "text": "not only discoverable, but also"}, {"start": 959.0, "text": "scans for BT devices."}, {"start": 962.0, "text": "Exactly as in the previous"}, {"start": 964.0, "text": "option, the driver enters this"}, {"start": 966.0, "text": "menu by either navigating the"}, {"start": 968.0, "text": "native UI to add a new Bluetooth"}, {"start": 970.0, "text": "device or by long pressing on"}, {"start": 973.0, "text": "the Voice Recognition button on"}, {"start": 975.0, "text": "the steering wheel."}, {"start": 977.0, "text": "Any BT capable device will be"}, {"start": 979.0, "text": "shown in this list, so the list"}, {"start": 981.0, "text": "might or might not include"}, {"start": 983.0, "text": "CarPlay devices."}, {"start": 985.0, "text": "That is why it is important to"}, {"start": 988.0, "text": "note that in this option any"}, {"start": 990.0, "text": "mention of Apple CarPlay on the"}, {"start": 992.0, "text": "UI is not recommended."}, {"start": 996.0, "text": "With this UI, the driver can"}, {"start": 998.0, "text": "select the device to pair to"}, {"start": 1001.0, "text": "from the native UI or as before"}, {"start": 1004.0, "text": "on the device."}, {"start": 1006.0, "text": "The third option is very"}, {"start": 1008.0, "text": "similar, however, this time the"}, {"start": 1011.0, "text": "user is explicitly adding a new"}, {"start": 1014.0, "text": "CarPlay device from the native"}, {"start": 1015.0, "text": "user interface."}, {"start": 1018.0, "text": "The list shows only devices that"}, {"start": 1020.0, "text": "actually support wireless"}, {"start": 1021.0, "text": "CarPlay."}, {"start": 1023.0, "text": "The head unit must use the Apple"}, {"start": 1025.0, "text": "CarPlay Bluetooth EIR to"}, {"start": 1027.0, "text": "accomplish this filtering."}, {"start": 1030.0, "text": "Again, as before, the driver"}, {"start": 1033.0, "text": "selects either on the car's UI"}, {"start": 1036.0, "text": "or on device."}, {"start": 1040.0, "text": "After a device has been selected"}, {"start": 1043.0, "text": "the head unit and iPhone"}, {"start": 1044.0, "text": "complete Bluetooth secure simple"}, {"start": 1046.0, "text": "pairing and connect IP over"}, {"start": 1048.0, "text": "Bluetooth and the head unit"}, {"start": 1050.0, "text": "identifies support for the"}, {"start": 1053.0, "text": "required messages."}, {"start": 1055.0, "text": "When iAP2 connects iOS will"}, {"start": 1058.0, "text": "prompt the user to enable"}, {"start": 1060.0, "text": "wireless CarPlay on device."}, {"start": 1063.0, "text": "And just as a side note, but a"}, {"start": 1064.0, "text": "very important one, connect"}, {"start": 1066.0, "text": "additional BT profiles only if"}, {"start": 1070.0, "text": "the wireless access point is"}, {"start": 1071.0, "text": "operating in the 5GHz band."}, {"start": 1075.0, "text": "Once iAP2 is connected iOS"}, {"start": 1079.0, "text": "provides the device transport"}, {"start": 1080.0, "text": "identifiers so that the head"}, {"start": 1082.0, "text": "unit can store the device as a"}, {"start": 1084.0, "text": "CarPlay device and recognize it"}, {"start": 1087.0, "text": "over a different transport when"}, {"start": 1089.0, "text": "it gets reconnected later on."}, {"start": 1092.0, "text": "The head unit listens to"}, {"start": 1093.0, "text": "wireless CarPlay update"}, {"start": 1094.0, "text": "notifications and if CarPlay is"}, {"start": 1097.0, "text": "enabled on device it may choose"}, {"start": 1100.0, "text": "to confirm whether to proceed"}, {"start": 1102.0, "text": "with setup for CarPlay."}, {"start": 1105.0, "text": "As we saw earlier, this"}, {"start": 1107.0, "text": "confirmation is only needed if"}, {"start": 1109.0, "text": "the user selected the device"}, {"start": 1112.0, "text": "through the add Bluetooth device"}, {"start": 1114.0, "text": "menus."}, {"start": 1116.0, "text": "As the user initiated pairing"}, {"start": 1118.0, "text": "through Bluetooth settings on"}, {"start": 1119.0, "text": "iPhone we see a similar"}, {"start": 1121.0, "text": "confirmation on iPhone as well."}, {"start": 1124.0, "text": "Of course, neither of those"}, {"start": 1127.0, "text": "confirmation dialogs will be"}, {"start": 1129.0, "text": "shown if the driver initiated"}, {"start": 1131.0, "text": "pairing from CarPlay specific"}, {"start": 1133.0, "text": "menus."}, {"start": 1136.0, "text": "Next, let's assume the user"}, {"start": 1138.0, "text": "confirms on the device first."}, {"start": 1141.0, "text": "When that happens the device"}, {"start": 1145.0, "text": "requests to receive the wireless"}, {"start": 1148.0, "text": "credentials of the Wi-Fi access"}, {"start": 1150.0, "text": "point."}, {"start": 1152.0, "text": "The head unit must wait for the"}, {"start": 1154.0, "text": "user confirmation before"}, {"start": 1155.0, "text": "responding."}, {"start": 1157.0, "text": "This is the time to get the"}, {"start": 1159.0, "text": "user's consent and if needed,"}, {"start": 1162.0, "text": "reconfigure the system for"}, {"start": 1163.0, "text": "wireless CarPlay."}, {"start": 1165.0, "text": "Now the user confirms on the"}, {"start": 1168.0, "text": "native UI as well."}, {"start": 1170.0, "text": "Then the head unit responds with"}, {"start": 1172.0, "text": "the credentials and iPhone"}, {"start": 1175.0, "text": "starts searching for the access"}, {"start": 1177.0, "text": "point and joins it."}, {"start": 1180.0, "text": "From now on, exactly ask for"}, {"start": 1182.0, "text": "wired CarPlay."}, {"start": 1184.0, "text": "Bonjour discovery runs and once"}, {"start": 1187.0, "text": "the device is found the head"}, {"start": 1189.0, "text": "unit initiates a CarPlay session"}, {"start": 1191.0, "text": "through CarPlay Control API."}, {"start": 1196.0, "text": "CarPlay session follows, as well"}, {"start": 1199.0, "text": "as connection establishment for"}, {"start": 1201.0, "text": "iAP2 over CarPlay."}, {"start": 1204.0, "text": "Note that at this point iAP2 is"}, {"start": 1207.0, "text": "also still connected over"}, {"start": 1210.0, "text": "Bluetooth."}, {"start": 1213.0, "text": "Then iPhone sends a disabled"}, {"start": 1215.0, "text": "Bluetooth command and the head"}, {"start": 1217.0, "text": "unit must disconnect all"}, {"start": 1219.0, "text": "Bluetooth connections to this"}, {"start": 1221.0, "text": "device."}, {"start": 1223.0, "text": "Remember that if the access"}, {"start": 1226.0, "text": "point is operating in the 2.4GHz"}, {"start": 1230.0, "text": "band Bluetooth needs to be"}, {"start": 1232.0, "text": "turned off while there's an"}, {"start": 1234.0, "text": "active CarPlay session to avoid"}, {"start": 1235.0, "text": "interference."}, {"start": 1239.0, "text": "Now that the screen and video"}, {"start": 1241.0, "text": "streams are started and the"}, {"start": 1242.0, "text": "CarPlay UI is visible on the"}, {"start": 1244.0, "text": "screen voila, CarPlay is running"}, {"start": 1247.0, "text": "without any wires."}, {"start": 1251.0, "text": "All right, now that we saw how"}, {"start": 1253.0, "text": "to set up wireless CarPlay"}, {"start": 1255.0, "text": "here's some general points to"}, {"start": 1257.0, "text": "consider."}, {"start": 1260.0, "text": "First, after setup is done the"}, {"start": 1262.0, "text": "CarPlay UI is expected to show"}, {"start": 1264.0, "text": "up."}, {"start": 1266.0, "text": "Then if iPhone is playing music,"}, {"start": 1269.0, "text": "music playback will be set up"}, {"start": 1271.0, "text": "through CarPlay."}, {"start": 1273.0, "text": "Lastly, the device must be"}, {"start": 1275.0, "text": "stored as the last connected BT"}, {"start": 1277.0, "text": "device so that it can be"}, {"start": 1279.0, "text": "reconnected automatically later"}, {"start": 1281.0, "text": "on."}, {"start": 1285.0, "text": "And with that we can conclude"}, {"start": 1286.0, "text": "the discussion around setup and"}, {"start": 1288.0, "text": "pairing and move to actually"}, {"start": 1291.0, "text": "look into how a CarPlay device"}, {"start": 1293.0, "text": "is connected when the user"}, {"start": 1295.0, "text": "returns to the car."}, {"start": 1297.0, "text": "When you reconnect for CarPlay"}, {"start": 1299.0, "text": "you need to take into account"}, {"start": 1301.0, "text": "all devices connected to the"}, {"start": 1302.0, "text": "system at the moment, as well as"}, {"start": 1306.0, "text": "the state of the system before"}, {"start": 1308.0, "text": "ignition was turned off."}, {"start": 1311.0, "text": "Whether CarPlay is using USB as"}, {"start": 1314.0, "text": "the transport or the wireless"}, {"start": 1316.0, "text": "link it's completely transparent"}, {"start": 1318.0, "text": "to the user and depends only on"}, {"start": 1321.0, "text": "how a device is connected to the"}, {"start": 1323.0, "text": "car and in which order the"}, {"start": 1325.0, "text": "connections happened."}, {"start": 1329.0, "text": "After deciding which device to"}, {"start": 1330.0, "text": "connect to make sure the device"}, {"start": 1333.0, "text": "still has CarPlay enabled."}, {"start": 1336.0, "text": "Revert to using legacy"}, {"start": 1338.0, "text": "technologies if CarPlay is no"}, {"start": 1340.0, "text": "longer available."}, {"start": 1343.0, "text": "Once the reconnection succeeds"}, {"start": 1346.0, "text": "restore how the user used the"}, {"start": 1348.0, "text": "system last time."}, {"start": 1350.0, "text": "If she was listening to FM radio"}, {"start": 1352.0, "text": "continue playing it."}, {"start": 1354.0, "text": "Show the last screen the user"}, {"start": 1356.0, "text": "was looking at either a native"}, {"start": 1358.0, "text": "application or CarPlay."}, {"start": 1361.0, "text": "The user experience should"}, {"start": 1362.0, "text": "simply continue and follow the"}, {"start": 1365.0, "text": "user's habit."}, {"start": 1368.0, "text": "Lastly, once a CarPlay session"}, {"start": 1370.0, "text": "is running on a device do not"}, {"start": 1373.0, "text": "interrupt it."}, {"start": 1375.0, "text": "Imagine the driver is listening"}, {"start": 1376.0, "text": "to her favorite song or"}, {"start": 1378.0, "text": "navigating and a friend plugs in"}, {"start": 1381.0, "text": "to charge it will be disruptive"}, {"start": 1383.0, "text": "if music all of a sudden resumed"}, {"start": 1385.0, "text": "from the friend's phone."}, {"start": 1388.0, "text": "Now let's review some scenarios"}, {"start": 1390.0, "text": "to better understand what it"}, {"start": 1392.0, "text": "means when we say the"}, {"start": 1394.0, "text": "reconnection depends on the"}, {"start": 1395.0, "text": "availability and the order of"}, {"start": 1397.0, "text": "events."}, {"start": 1399.0, "text": "In all these scenarios, we"}, {"start": 1401.0, "text": "assume that the phone has been"}, {"start": 1403.0, "text": "previously paired for wireless"}, {"start": 1404.0, "text": "CarPlay and the system has at"}, {"start": 1407.0, "text": "least one USB port."}, {"start": 1410.0, "text": "We are going to pay attention to"}, {"start": 1412.0, "text": "when iPhone was connected over"}, {"start": 1413.0, "text": "USB, identify a common scenario,"}, {"start": 1417.0, "text": "and observe which transport is"}, {"start": 1419.0, "text": "used to establish a CarPlay"}, {"start": 1420.0, "text": "session."}, {"start": 1423.0, "text": "First, let's look at the"}, {"start": 1424.0, "text": "scenario where there is just one"}, {"start": 1427.0, "text": "iPhone in the car."}, {"start": 1429.0, "text": "The simplest situation is that"}, {"start": 1431.0, "text": "the user gets back into the car"}, {"start": 1434.0, "text": "for a short drive and keeps"}, {"start": 1436.0, "text": "iPhone in the pocket."}, {"start": 1438.0, "text": "A morning commute running small"}, {"start": 1440.0, "text": "errands would be the perfect"}, {"start": 1442.0, "text": "examples."}, {"start": 1444.0, "text": "As the only available transport"}, {"start": 1446.0, "text": "is wireless naturally CarPlay"}, {"start": 1449.0, "text": "runs wirelessly."}, {"start": 1453.0, "text": "In the next scenario, the driver"}, {"start": 1456.0, "text": "plugs in after the drive has"}, {"start": 1457.0, "text": "started."}, {"start": 1459.0, "text": "Typical usage here is just"}, {"start": 1461.0, "text": "realizing that the phone needs"}, {"start": 1464.0, "text": "to be charged after departing."}, {"start": 1468.0, "text": "In this case, the session has"}, {"start": 1470.0, "text": "already started over wireless"}, {"start": 1472.0, "text": "and since we do not want any"}, {"start": 1474.0, "text": "interruptions CarPlay remains"}, {"start": 1476.0, "text": "over wireless."}, {"start": 1478.0, "text": "In the next scenario, the user"}, {"start": 1480.0, "text": "simply leaves the phone plugged"}, {"start": 1482.0, "text": "in and gets out of the car."}, {"start": 1486.0, "text": "This could be a stopover at the"}, {"start": 1487.0, "text": "gas station or simply forgetting"}, {"start": 1489.0, "text": "the phone in the car."}, {"start": 1492.0, "text": "Now when the user returns the"}, {"start": 1494.0, "text": "device is available to connect"}, {"start": 1496.0, "text": "over both USB and wireless."}, {"start": 1499.0, "text": "However, usually the USB stack"}, {"start": 1503.0, "text": "resumes faster so CarPlay is"}, {"start": 1505.0, "text": "reconnected over USB."}, {"start": 1507.0, "text": "Now let's look at what happens"}, {"start": 1509.0, "text": "if the driver plugs in right"}, {"start": 1511.0, "text": "after entering the car."}, {"start": 1514.0, "text": "This could be when leaving for a"}, {"start": 1516.0, "text": "longer trip or maybe needing to"}, {"start": 1518.0, "text": "charge right away."}, {"start": 1521.0, "text": "In this case, as the system is"}, {"start": 1523.0, "text": "coming up it will bring up both"}, {"start": 1526.0, "text": "the USB and wireless stacks."}, {"start": 1529.0, "text": "Since the timing will depend"}, {"start": 1530.0, "text": "heavily on the user's behavior"}, {"start": 1533.0, "text": "the CarPlay session will be"}, {"start": 1534.0, "text": "started over the first available"}, {"start": 1536.0, "text": "transport."}, {"start": 1538.0, "text": "If USB is up while BT or Wi-Fi"}, {"start": 1542.0, "text": "are still reconnecting the"}, {"start": 1543.0, "text": "session will end up being over"}, {"start": 1545.0, "text": "USB."}, {"start": 1546.0, "text": "If wireless reconnected before"}, {"start": 1548.0, "text": "USB then the session will run"}, {"start": 1550.0, "text": "over wireless."}, {"start": 1555.0, "text": "In the last scenario, we"}, {"start": 1557.0, "text": "consider multiple devices in the"}, {"start": 1558.0, "text": "car."}, {"start": 1560.0, "text": "The driver might have plugged in"}, {"start": 1562.0, "text": "right after entering the car."}, {"start": 1566.0, "text": "This could be a road trip with"}, {"start": 1567.0, "text": "friends that need to charge at"}, {"start": 1569.0, "text": "some point or want to play music"}, {"start": 1571.0, "text": "from their phones."}, {"start": 1573.0, "text": "Again, as before, the session"}, {"start": 1575.0, "text": "will initially start depending"}, {"start": 1577.0, "text": "on the available transport."}, {"start": 1581.0, "text": "Later on, the driver might"}, {"start": 1582.0, "text": "decide to change the active"}, {"start": 1584.0, "text": "CarPlay device using the native"}, {"start": 1586.0, "text": "user interface."}, {"start": 1589.0, "text": "All right, now let's see how you"}, {"start": 1592.0, "text": "can implement all these"}, {"start": 1593.0, "text": "scenarios."}, {"start": 1595.0, "text": "We can start by looking at the"}, {"start": 1597.0, "text": "flow for wireless reconnection."}, {"start": 1601.0, "text": "First, wait until both Bluetooth"}, {"start": 1604.0, "text": "and the access point are fully"}, {"start": 1606.0, "text": "operational."}, {"start": 1609.0, "text": "Then check that the last"}, {"start": 1611.0, "text": "connected device is marked for"}, {"start": 1613.0, "text": "CarPlay on the head unit."}, {"start": 1614.0, "text": "If it is, make sure that there"}, {"start": 1619.0, "text": "is no other active CarPlay"}, {"start": 1621.0, "text": "session either with the same"}, {"start": 1623.0, "text": "device or with another wired or"}, {"start": 1626.0, "text": "wireless device."}, {"start": 1629.0, "text": "If there is no other session"}, {"start": 1631.0, "text": "proceed with connecting iAP2"}, {"start": 1634.0, "text": "over Bluetooth."}, {"start": 1637.0, "text": "Once iAP2 Is connected wait to"}, {"start": 1640.0, "text": "receive a notification that"}, {"start": 1642.0, "text": "wireless CarPlay is enabled."}, {"start": 1646.0, "text": "If it is wait for the device to"}, {"start": 1649.0, "text": "be discovered and connect."}, {"start": 1653.0, "text": "When the connect command is"}, {"start": 1655.0, "text": "issued iPhone will check which"}, {"start": 1657.0, "text": "interfaces are available and"}, {"start": 1660.0, "text": "will initiate the session either"}, {"start": 1663.0, "text": "over wireless or wired."}, {"start": 1666.0, "text": "Moving on to USB the flow looks"}, {"start": 1669.0, "text": "fairly similar."}, {"start": 1670.0, "text": "You wait until the device gets"}, {"start": 1672.0, "text": "connected, you check that there"}, {"start": 1675.0, "text": "is no active session as we do"}, {"start": 1677.0, "text": "not want to interrupt it."}, {"start": 1679.0, "text": "If there is none check that"}, {"start": 1681.0, "text": "CarPlay is enabled."}, {"start": 1683.0, "text": "Then proceed with your role"}, {"start": 1684.0, "text": "switch and selecting a device to"}, {"start": 1687.0, "text": "connect. At this point again, iPhone"}, {"start": 1691.0, "text": "checks if both the wireless and"}, {"start": 1693.0, "text": "wired link are available and"}, {"start": 1695.0, "text": "picks one of the two to"}, {"start": 1697.0, "text": "establish the session."}, {"start": 1700.0, "text": "Then last user mode is restored"}, {"start": 1702.0, "text": "and the driver is all set."}, {"start": 1706.0, "text": "In the previous two slides, we"}, {"start": 1708.0, "text": "saw how to automatically"}, {"start": 1709.0, "text": "reconnect to the last used"}, {"start": 1711.0, "text": "device."}, {"start": 1713.0, "text": "But what happens if there are"}, {"start": 1714.0, "text": "multiple CarPlay devices in the"}, {"start": 1716.0, "text": "vehicle?"}, {"start": 1718.0, "text": "They might be connected just"}, {"start": 1720.0, "text": "over USB, just paired for"}, {"start": 1723.0, "text": "wireless or both paired for"}, {"start": 1726.0, "text": "wireless and connected over USB."}, {"start": 1729.0, "text": "One of those devices will get"}, {"start": 1731.0, "text": "reconnected automatically, but"}, {"start": 1733.0, "text": "as we mentioned before, the"}, {"start": 1736.0, "text": "native UI lists all devices and"}, {"start": 1739.0, "text": "lets the driver change the"}, {"start": 1740.0, "text": "active CarPlay device."}, {"start": 1744.0, "text": "When that happens, the head unit"}, {"start": 1746.0, "text": "follows the same procedures to"}, {"start": 1748.0, "text": "reconnect over the available"}, {"start": 1749.0, "text": "transport."}, {"start": 1752.0, "text": "Lastly, let's talk about"}, {"start": 1754.0, "text": "reconnecting after a session"}, {"start": 1755.0, "text": "disconnect."}, {"start": 1757.0, "text": "CarPlay disconnection might"}, {"start": 1759.0, "text": "occur for multiple reasons."}, {"start": 1761.0, "text": "The head unit must be aware why"}, {"start": 1763.0, "text": "the disconnection happened and"}, {"start": 1765.0, "text": "determine if a reconnect is"}, {"start": 1767.0, "text": "required. Here are a couple of common"}, {"start": 1770.0, "text": "scenarios and expected outcome."}, {"start": 1774.0, "text": "In situations where the user"}, {"start": 1777.0, "text": "unplugs from USB or manually"}, {"start": 1779.0, "text": "disconnects from the native UI."}, {"start": 1782.0, "text": "No reconnection is needed as"}, {"start": 1784.0, "text": "there was an explicit user"}, {"start": 1786.0, "text": "action to terminate the CarPlay"}, {"start": 1790.0, "text": "session."}, {"start": 1791.0, "text": "However, if the phone is no"}, {"start": 1793.0, "text": "longer reachable for example,"}, {"start": 1796.0, "text": "the user walks away, turns off"}, {"start": 1798.0, "text": "Wi-Fi or anything similar, the"}, {"start": 1801.0, "text": "head unit is expected to do a"}, {"start": 1803.0, "text": "fast reconnect to the same"}, {"start": 1805.0, "text": "device using CarPlay Control"}, {"start": 1807.0, "text": "API."}, {"start": 1808.0, "text": "If that fails then proceed with"}, {"start": 1811.0, "text": "the Bluetooth reconnect to"}, {"start": 1813.0, "text": "reestablish the CarPlay session."}, {"start": 1817.0, "text": "With this we have explored all"}, {"start": 1819.0, "text": "types of CarPlay connections."}, {"start": 1822.0, "text": "Now let's go over some"}, {"start": 1823.0, "text": "architectural considerations"}, {"start": 1825.0, "text": "when designing a wireless"}, {"start": 1826.0, "text": "CarPlay system."}, {"start": 1830.0, "text": "When designing a wireless"}, {"start": 1832.0, "text": "system, you want to optimize for"}, {"start": 1833.0, "text": "performance."}, {"start": 1836.0, "text": "That means that you have to"}, {"start": 1838.0, "text": "decide which Wi-Fi protocol to"}, {"start": 1841.0, "text": "support, what configuration to"}, {"start": 1844.0, "text": "use and in which frequency band"}, {"start": 1846.0, "text": "to operate."}, {"start": 1849.0, "text": "Next, you need to think about"}, {"start": 1851.0, "text": "what other wireless technologies"}, {"start": 1853.0, "text": "will be used in the vehicle and"}, {"start": 1855.0, "text": "potential interferences."}, {"start": 1860.0, "text": "Services like Internet data or"}, {"start": 1862.0, "text": "other in-car applications might"}, {"start": 1865.0, "text": "also have an impact on the"}, {"start": 1867.0, "text": "performance."}, {"start": 1870.0, "text": "With all that in mind you need"}, {"start": 1872.0, "text": "to assure that the wireless"}, {"start": 1874.0, "text": "performance requirements for"}, {"start": 1875.0, "text": "CarPlay are satisfied."}, {"start": 1878.0, "text": "So, what do we recommend for"}, {"start": 1879.0, "text": "wireless CarPlay?"}, {"start": 1881.0, "text": "First, we really recommend that"}, {"start": 1883.0, "text": "your wireless access point"}, {"start": 1884.0, "text": "operates in the 5GHz band."}, {"start": 1887.0, "text": "It offers more channels to"}, {"start": 1889.0, "text": "choose from, it's less prone to"}, {"start": 1891.0, "text": "interference, and it is the"}, {"start": 1894.0, "text": "least congested band."}, {"start": 1896.0, "text": "Please do use 5GHz whenever"}, {"start": 1899.0, "text": "possible."}, {"start": 1904.0, "text": "Even though 2.4GHz is not"}, {"start": 1906.0, "text": "recommended and is highly"}, {"start": 1908.0, "text": "congested in some regulatory"}, {"start": 1911.0, "text": "domains you might have to use"}, {"start": 1913.0, "text": "it."}, {"start": 1914.0, "text": "Then you need to be very aware"}, {"start": 1917.0, "text": "of coexistent scenarios and you"}, {"start": 1920.0, "text": "must disable the Bluetooth stack"}, {"start": 1922.0, "text": "completely while there is an"}, {"start": 1924.0, "text": "active CarPlay session."}, {"start": 1927.0, "text": "If you offer LTE connectivity on"}, {"start": 1930.0, "text": "Band 40 your choices of"}, {"start": 1932.0, "text": "operating channels become even"}, {"start": 1935.0, "text": "more limited."}, {"start": 1938.0, "text": "Remember if you are designing a"}, {"start": 1940.0, "text": "system which will operate in"}, {"start": 1942.0, "text": "both bands you need to consider"}, {"start": 1945.0, "text": "how the user experience will be"}, {"start": 1946.0, "text": "impacted."}, {"start": 1948.0, "text": "In 5GHz other Bluetooth devices"}, {"start": 1951.0, "text": "may be paired and connected in"}, {"start": 1952.0, "text": "parallel, whereas in 2.4GHz,"}, {"start": 1956.0, "text": "adding or connecting a second"}, {"start": 1958.0, "text": "Bluetooth device is not"}, {"start": 1960.0, "text": "possible."}, {"start": 1965.0, "text": "Some systems might choose to"}, {"start": 1966.0, "text": "deploy multiple access points or"}, {"start": 1968.0, "text": "dual band APs to offer a variety"}, {"start": 1971.0, "text": "of in-car services and"}, {"start": 1972.0, "text": "applications."}, {"start": 1975.0, "text": "If these access points are"}, {"start": 1977.0, "text": "operating in the same frequency"}, {"start": 1978.0, "text": "band they need to use different"}, {"start": 1980.0, "text": "channels to avoid interference."}, {"start": 1984.0, "text": "If the access points use the"}, {"start": 1987.0, "text": "same SSID and password they need"}, {"start": 1990.0, "text": "to offer the same set of"}, {"start": 1992.0, "text": "services to prevent inconsistent"}, {"start": 1994.0, "text": "experience."}, {"start": 1996.0, "text": "And lastly, using hidden"}, {"start": 1998.0, "text": "networks is not recommended for"}, {"start": 2001.0, "text": "CarPlay."}, {"start": 2005.0, "text": "Finally, let's look at how to"}, {"start": 2007.0, "text": "provide Internet data"}, {"start": 2009.0, "text": "connectivity to iPhone."}, {"start": 2011.0, "text": "The head unit communicates the"}, {"start": 2013.0, "text": "state of the Internet"}, {"start": 2015.0, "text": "connectivity dynamically through"}, {"start": 2017.0, "text": "the Apple Device IE and through"}, {"start": 2020.0, "text": "the Networking IE."}, {"start": 2023.0, "text": "Notifications need to descend on"}, {"start": 2025.0, "text": "changes."}, {"start": 2027.0, "text": "For example, to state that the"}, {"start": 2029.0, "text": "data communication module is"}, {"start": 2031.0, "text": "available on the system or that"}, {"start": 2034.0, "text": "there is a failure with that"}, {"start": 2035.0, "text": "module or that the service"}, {"start": 2039.0, "text": "contract has expired."}, {"start": 2042.0, "text": "Temporary loss of connection due"}, {"start": 2045.0, "text": "to poor cell coverage does not"}, {"start": 2047.0, "text": "need to be communicated to"}, {"start": 2048.0, "text": "iPhone."}, {"start": 2051.0, "text": "For more information about this"}, {"start": 2052.0, "text": "session check out the session"}, {"start": 2054.0, "text": "website."}, {"start": 2056.0, "text": "If you're interested in"}, {"start": 2057.0, "text": "developing CarPlay apps check"}, {"start": 2059.0, "text": "out the Enabling Your App for"}, {"start": 2061.0, "text": "CarPlay session."}, {"start": 2063.0, "text": "Also, refer to the videos from"}, {"start": 2065.0, "text": "last year for basic information"}]}
